{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T23:57:21.549Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_JvEgKHyIEDJuWbACtgJClKOP","output":"Chunk ID: e8e85d\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 2156\nOutput:\n     1\t// Package review — see env.go for package-level rationale.\n     2\t//\n     3\t// run_multi.go implements RunMulti, the N-agent orchestrator. It runs each\n     4\t// AgentReviewer in its own goroutine under a shared context, fans their\n     5\t// event streams into a single dispatch loop that calls each Sink serially\n     6\t// (preserving the serial-dispatch contract from CU4), and aggregates the\n     7\t// per-agent results into a single RunSummary.\n     8\t//\n     9\t// Cancellation: when ctx is cancelled (typically by the cobra command's\n    10\t// SIGINT handling), all per-agent reviewers see ctx.Err() via their\n    11\t// individual Process implementations and exit. RunMulti waits for every\n    12\t// goroutine to drain before returning, ensuring no AgentEvent calls fire\n    13\t// after RunFinished.\n    14\t//\n    15\t// Goroutine accounting for N agents:\n    16\t//   - N forwarding goroutines: one per agent that started successfully,\n    17\t//     reads proc.Events() and sends tagged events to the fan-in channel.\n    18\t//   - 1 channel-close goroutine: waits for all N forwarders via WaitGroup\n    19\t//     then closes the fan-in channel so the dispatch loop terminates.\n    20\t//   - 1 dispatch goroutine (the caller's): ranges over fan-in, updates\n    21\t//     per-agent state, calls sinks serially. RunMulti does NOT spawn a\n    22\t//     separate dispatch goroutine — the fan-in loop runs on the RunMulti\n    23\t//     call stack, keeping the goroutine count low.\n    24\tpackage review\n    25\t\n    26\timport (\n    27\t\t\"context\"\n    28\t\t\"sync\"\n    29\t\t\"time\"\n    30\t\n    31\t\treviewtypes \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/review/types\"\n    32\t)\n    33\t\n    34\t// perAgentState tracks the mutable accumulation for one agent during a\n    35\t// multi-agent run.\n    36\t//\n    37\t// Write paths (no mutex; the close-after-wait protocol below provides\n    38\t// happens-before for both):\n    39\t//   - waitErr and finishedAt are written by the per-agent forwarding\n    40\t//     goroutine after its proc.Events range loop exits, immediately before\n    41\t//     wg.Done.\n    42\t//   - All other mutable fields (events buffer, tokens, finishedSeen,\n    43\t//     finishedOk, sawRunError) are written from the single dispatch loop\n    44\t//     reading the fan-in channel.\n    45\t//\n    46\t// Read path: the main RunMulti goroutine reads every field only after\n    47\t// `for ev := range fanIn` returns, which is sequenced after wg.Wait →\n    48\t// close(fanIn) by the close goroutine. That sequencing is the\n    49\t// happens-before for both write paths.\n    50\t//\n    51\t// DO NOT add new writers from goroutines outside this protocol — adding\n    52\t// a third write path would require a mutex (or a redesign).\n    53\ttype perAgentState struct {\n    54\t\tname         string\n    55\t\tproc         reviewtypes.Process\n    56\t\tstartErr     error\n    57\t\tstartedAt    time.Time\n    58\t\tfinishedAt   time.Time\n    59\t\tbuffer       []reviewtypes.Event\n    60\t\ttokens       reviewtypes.Tokens\n    61\t\tfinishedSeen bool\n    62\t\tfinishedOk   bool\n    63\t\tsawRunError  bool\n    64\t\twaitErr      error\n    65\t}\n    66\t\n    67\t// taggedEvent associates a fan-in event with its originating agent index.\n    68\ttype taggedEvent struct {\n    69\t\tagentIdx int\n    70\t\tev       reviewtypes.Event\n    71\t}\n    72\t\n    73\t// RunMulti executes a multi-agent review. Each reviewer runs concurrently;\n    74\t// events from N agents are funneled into a single dispatch loop that calls\n    75\t// every sink's AgentEvent in arrival order from a single goroutine\n    76\t// (serial-dispatch guarantee).\n    77\t//\n    78\t// Returns the aggregated RunSummary plus the FIRST non-cancellation\n    79\t// per-agent error encountered. Callers that want individual errors should\n    80\t// inspect summary.AgentRuns[i].Err. The returned summary is always\n    81\t// populated, even on error; sinks are always notified via RunFinished.\n    82\t//\n    83\t// Cancellation propagates through ctx; each reviewer's Process honors it.\n    84\t// When ctx is cancelled all per-agent goroutines will eventually drain and\n    85\t// the channel will close; RunMulti waits for all before calling RunFinished.\n    86\tfunc RunMulti(\n    87\t\tctx context.Context,\n    88\t\treviewers []reviewtypes.AgentReviewer,\n    89\t\tcfg reviewtypes.RunConfig,\n    90\t\tsinks []reviewtypes.Sink,\n    91\t) (reviewtypes.RunSummary, error) {\n    92\t\tstarted := time.Now()\n    93\t\n    94\t\tif len(reviewers) == 0 {\n    95\t\t\tsummary := reviewtypes.RunSummary{\n    96\t\t\t\tStartedAt:  started,\n    97\t\t\t\tFinishedAt: started,\n    98\t\t\t\tCancelled:  ctx.Err() != nil,\n    99\t\t\t}\n   100\t\t\tfor _, sink := range sinks {\n   101\t\t\t\tsink.RunFinished(summary)\n   102\t\t\t}\n   103\t\t\treturn summary, nil\n   104\t\t}\n   105\t\n   106\t\tstates := make([]*perAgentState, len(reviewers))\n   107\t\tfor i, r := range reviewers {\n   108\t\t\tstates[i] = &perAgentState{\n   109\t\t\t\tname:      r.Name(),\n   110\t\t\t\tstartedAt: time.Now(),\n   111\t\t\t}\n   112\t\t}\n   113\t\n   114\t\t// fanIn carries tagged events from N agent goroutines into the single\n   115\t\t// dispatch loop. Buffer of len(reviewers)*16 amortises goroutine\n   116\t\t// scheduling jitter without holding an unbounded queue.\n   117\t\tfanIn := make(chan taggedEvent, len(reviewers)*16)\n   118\t\n   119\t\tvar wg sync.WaitGroup\n   120\t\tfor i, r := range reviewers {\n   121\t\t\tproc, err := r.Start(ctx, cfg)\n   122\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   123\t\t\t\tstates